        "original_id": "9e4bba9b-db04-57ac-8a08-0d05b79c6c22",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Competitions: Football League Super Cup, ScreenSport Super Cup, European tournaments, 1985 European Cup Final\n- Organizations: Football League, UEFA\n- Events: Heysel Stadium disaster\n- Places: England, Heysel Stadium, Brussels, Belgium\n- Clubs: Juventus, Liverpool\n\nFacts:\n- On 29 May 1985, the Heysel Stadium disaster occurred at Heysel Stadium in Brussels, Belgium, before the 1985 European Cup Final between Juventus of Italy and Liverpool of England.\n- The Heysel Stadium disaster led UEFA to ban English clubs from entering European tournaments.\n- In the 1985–86 season in England, the Football League Super Cup was held as a one-off football club competition.\n- The Football League Super Cup was later known by the sponsored name ScreenSport Super Cup.\n- The Football League organized the Football League Super Cup as financial and sporting compensation for English clubs that had qualified for European competition in the previous season but were barred by UEFA after the Heysel Stadium disaster.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b748e1fe-bb7d-5659-a4b5-9927f4a8830d",
        "text": "Page: Football League Super Cup. Sentence: The Football League Super Cup (later known under its sponsored name as the ScreenSport Super Cup) was a one-off football club competition held in England in the 1985–86 season.\nPage: Football League Super Cup. Sentence: It was organised by the Football League and was intended as some form of financial and sporting compensation for the English clubs which had qualified for European competition in the previous season but had been banned from entering European tournaments by UEFA following the Heysel Stadium disaster.\nPage: Heysel Stadium disaster. Sentence: The Heysel Stadium disaster (] , ] ; Dutch: \"Heizeldrama\" ; French: \"Drame du Heysel\" ) occurred on 29 May 1985 when escaping fans were pressed against a collapsing wall in the Heysel Stadium in Brussels, Belgium, before the start of the 1985 European Cup Final between Juventus of Italy and Liverpool of England.",
